       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), which is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily. This may be where the \"1600\" came from.\n\nIf you do want the dose as written, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
